Google Pixel 8 Pro (husky, Tensor G3 "zuma") on a mainline kernel
(github.com/Noxyntious/linux, branch port/google-husky).

vendor/ztos/manifest.toml  ztOSIAL manifest (zrnperfd CPU ceilings, power limit)
overlay/                   rootfs files the port adds on top of the ztOS image:
  ztos-autosleep           suspend-to-RAM while the screen is off; Wi-Fi powered down
                           through brcmfmac's wlan_power around sleep; stays awake while
                           audio plays
  ztos-call-audio          routes call audio through the AoC while a call is up
  ztos-husky-hw            boot-time hardware setup (Wi-Fi MAC, ...)
  ztos-boot-successful     marks the A/B slot successful (no fall back to slot a)
  husky-charge-thermal     throttles charging by battery temperature
  ztos-waydroid-screen     puts Waydroid's Android to sleep with the screen (KEYCODE_SLEEP/
                           WAKEUP), so apps stop rendering on the GPU in the pocket
  60-husky-skin-thermal    makes the kernel's skin-thermal zone (battery thermistor, IPA
                           on all CPU clusters + GPU, 41 C) proportional-only
  ztos-husky-noc2.conf     cpu8 (X3) C2 off: ACPM hangs otherwise
  60-flatpak-gl.conf       Flatpak apps use the "husky" GL extension (tools/flatpak-gl)
  btaddr: build tools/btaddr.c for aarch64 into usr/local/libexec/btaddr
tools/                     flatpak-gl (Mesa 26.3 GL extension recipe), green-capture.sh
                           (display state snapshot, needs mmrd.c + dqedump.sh)
Not here (proprietary or carrier data): firmware, modem images, ims.db.
